<%# What this broker stores and for how long. %>
<main>
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>kyc.demo.kiosk.tech is a demo of a KYC provider for Kiosk operators. It has no accounts. This page says what it
    stores and for how long.</p>
  <h2>What it stores</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Verification requests.</strong> For each check that an operator opens: the operator, its callback
      address, the facts it asks for, its own id for you (an opaque id, never a name or an e-mail address), a nonce,
      the status and when the request expires, 15 minutes after it opens.</li>
    <li><strong>Nothing about you.</strong> We never store the facts you confirm, a document, a name or a date of
      birth. We sign the answer and send it to the operator, and we keep no copy. While the operator does not accept
      it, the answer stays in this server's memory for at most a minute, so that we can send it again.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>Each request writes a log line with its path, its parameters and the IP address it came from. The server's
    system journal keeps these lines until it deletes its oldest lines to stay below its size limit.</p>
  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>We keep verification requests until we delete them by hand, with no fixed schedule.</p>
</main>
